{"schema": "columns@1", "language": "german", "notes": ["German column of the meaning matrix. Written for this project. Tokens are [text, \"\", meaning id]: German is written in the Latin alphabet, so there is no separate reading. Nouns keep their capitals.", "Subject pronouns are always written, so nothing is implied. Fixed phrases that carry one meaning are one token (Freut mich, Es regnet, tut weh, nach Hause, Lass uns). zur is zu + der and carries @direction+@the.", "\"Wie spät ist es?\" asks the time and \"Wie viel ist das?\" asks the price, so \"Wie viel\" always means how-much.", "Code rows use the infinitive at the end (Das Wort ausgeben.), the usual form for instructions in German software and manuals. It also keeps separable verbs (ausgeben, zurückgeben) in one piece."], "sep": " "}
